DE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection/ec0cc3e570302f305d75fac15c6c9d7a44f23365dfe34b065a9b46d1aae32455" :answer/id #uuid "ae0d096a-2522-5ff0-a17d-ed868c61e17f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection/d75ef8342eba9af6801b05734c4d986ad60ea9fba778193ff6c00fd77bc6c74b" :answer/id #uuid "dbe214a8-c8ac-5d10-b793-cc97e74c1bf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection/429a08e42bdf456e504f7c7682d29e6aa92b48898e4e7ca8e14effd9110aeb56" :answer/id #uuid "634dec06-3b47-5c24-8b2d-3ef78d6de87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y={e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection/4675beea180c195b3c170149375d05ffee0fe8717b69e99ac9901ea76e81204e" :answer/id #uuid "cea1dc7a-0c4b-575b-aa74-2dd609fb1b9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection/214bd9a1df36f3d65e50bf05dda37ee798b9d7561bcfcc303770e87c877b3c1c" :answer/id #uuid "0f87f4c9-db69-5310-b5e7-ecd975161900" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8367e86-2a93-5802-b40f-6ccdd04f329b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103559/selection/214bd9a1df36f3d65e50bf05dda37ee798b9d7561bcfcc303770e87c877b3c1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-103559/selection/ec0cc3e570302f305d75fac15c6c9d7a44f23365dfe34b065a9b46d1aae32455" "q-103559/selection/d75ef8342eba9af6801b05734c4d986ad60ea9fba778193ff6c00fd77bc6c74b" "q-103559/selection/429a08e42bdf456e504f7c7682d29e6aa92b48898e4e7ca8e14effd9110aeb56" "q-103559/selection/4675beea180c195b3c170149375d05ffee0fe8717b69e99ac9901ea76e81204e" "q-103559/selection/214bd9a1df36f3d65e50bf05dda37ee798b9d7561bcfcc303770e87c877b3c1c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103559" :question/id #uuid "4f6f3d9f-1dcd-5dfc-ad09-04a9f798bb93" :question/math-academy-id "q-103559" :question/problem "Which of the following is **NOT** a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)={x}^{2}\n$$\n\ncannot be written in standard form since the power of $y$ in the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)$ is not $1.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103559/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103559"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103557/selection/4c8560d7b628f6a612d09e35ad5d22d61d6f41716f56b0757e3b0f70108a7c46" :answer/id #uuid "88ae4463-08e0-520a-