c{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy={y}^{2}\n$$\n\ncannot be written in standard form since the right-hand side depends on $y.$ Since the equation cannot be written in standard form, we conclude that it is not a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations can be written in the standard form, and therefore they are first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79750/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79750"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection/2d57c6e97d682caccce5e8f3e5dc752f6eba000e0398ecf4d9cfec575b0e7cb6" :answer/id #uuid "0d0692bd-bd42-52cf-a2ae-91371e3aa073" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y-x}{{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection/322d8481048ca0fc5833092de5837f4c302f8ef926c9f6603b28b4152f488999" :answer/id #uuid "5b7b52c0-c9b5-553d-82dc-5e67fbc14823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection/759dfd694dc3b891fb9b095ad56045f28010fa61175b2cb6617e0903ff289812" :answer/id #uuid "6da0902d-c64e-5abc-b9d3-c24e178f8591" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection/079c189395009be07b639d4d18d8036f3baa8b194c7968a9a816e7fab3cd719e" :answer/id #uuid "002576cf-2ed9-5b4b-85f5-930244d59605" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}+3x}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection/ae9810fa5550c12a180c95cc3d9523205e2343cb695bd1818c89e80ffbfbd248" :answer/id #uuid "d2a1ecc5-ec11-54dc-a466-7ca7e0f11cdc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "10b53c59-d11e-5e30-896d-6442479255cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79754/selection/759dfd694dc3b891fb9b095ad56045f28010fa61175b2cb6617e0903ff289812" :answer-field/choices ["q-79754/selection/2d57c6e97d682caccce5e8f3e5dc752f6eba000e0398ecf4d9cfec575b0e7cb6" "q-79754/selection/322d8481048ca0fc5833092de5837f4c302f8ef926c9f6603b28b4152f488999" "q-79754/selection/759dfd694dc3b891fb9b095ad56045f28010fa61175b2cb6617e0903ff289812" "q-79754/selection/079c189395009be07b639d4d18d8036f3baa8b194c7968a9a816e7fab3cd719e" "q-79754/selection/ae9810fa5550c12a180c95cc3d9523205e2343cb695bd1818c89e80ffbfbd248"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79754" :question/id #uuid "438bd143-91da-5d1a-8869-3ed754e59004" :question/math-academy-id "q-79754" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\frac{2y+{x}^{2}}{y}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2y+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is in standard form with  $P(x)=-2$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-79754/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d5d29575-c29b-56fe-af62-9f3fab6e0818" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "28dc1cdf-dce1-503b-b046-0ff022affc17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b27b7a48-7b2f-5251-afb0-8fef0d46a904" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "5cf227c3-f20d-5d7f-9976-825b249bfda5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9f554a0b-7bff-54aa-bab2-e475db2cf532" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "498d53ab-9a70-5608-b2fc-0ccb36cb644b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331738/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331738/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-331738/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-331738/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-331738/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-331738/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331738" :question/id #uuid "c2e6adcc-e613-5599-bfa6-8b950fbde93e" :question/math-academy-id "q-331738" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=2$\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=y$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=2$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+4xy & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+4xy-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(4x-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739a8f10-413a-5a1d-a47e-4afd0b14eb44"] :knowledge-point/questions 